00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:01,600
19 · Just Live a Good Life?

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,000
19 · Just Live a Good Life?
Can’t I just live a good life without believing in Jesus?

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Can’t I just live a good life without believing in Jesus?

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:11,600
Suppose you’re aboard a pirate ship.

5
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:18,600
No matter how spotless you keep the deck, how kind you are to the crew, how exemplary your life —

6
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:19,600
you are still a pirate,

7
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:22,400
Can’t I just live a good life without believing in Jesus?
you are still a pirate,

8
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:23,200
you are still a pirate,

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,800
because you’re carried along with the ship to where it’s headed (the harbor of judgment).

10
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:30,600
The problem is not a “score of behavior” but “which ship you belong to” (your identity).

11
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:36,200
Can’t I just live a good life without believing in Jesus?
The problem is not a “score of behavior” but “which ship you belong to” (your identity).

12
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:42,600
So the gospel doesn’t say “try harder to be good”; it says “change ships.”

13
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:43,600
Get off the ship of sin and cross over to Jesus — into the new identity of a child of God.

14
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:49,200
Can’t I just live a good life without believing in Jesus?
Get off the ship of sin and cross over to Jesus — into the new identity of a child of God.

15
